@startuml Basic Factory Method Pattern

' Define the styles
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontStyle bold
skinparam classBackgroundColor #f8f9fa
skinparam classBorderColor #dee2e6
skinparam arrowColor #6c757d
skinparam stereotypeCBackgroundColor #e9ecef

' Title
title Basic Factory Method Pattern - Core Structure

' Abstract Creator
abstract class CommissionCalculatorFactory <<Creator>> {
  {abstract} #createCommissionCalculation(dealId: String, salesRepId: String, amount: BigDecimal): CommissionCalculation
  +calculateCommission(dealId: String, salesRepId: String, amount: BigDecimal): CommissionCalculation
}

' Product Class
class CommissionCalculation <<Product>> {
  -id: String
  -dealId: String
  -salesRepId: String
  -baseCommission: BigDecimal
  -calculatedBy: String
  +recalculate(): void
  +setBaseCommission(amount: BigDecimal): void
}

' Concrete Creators
class StandardCommissionCalculatorFactory <<ConcreteCreator>> {
  #createCommissionCalculation(dealId: String, salesRepId: String, amount: BigDecimal): CommissionCalculation
  --
  <i>Creates "STANDARD-" prefixed calculations</i>
  <i>Uses base amount as-is</i>
}

class BonusCommissionCalculatorFactory <<ConcreteCreator>> {
  #createCommissionCalculation(dealId: String, salesRepId: String, amount: BigDecimal): CommissionCalculation
  --
  <i>Creates "BONUS-" prefixed calculations</i>
  <i>Applies 10% bonus to base amount</i>
}

class AcceleratedCommissionCalculatorFactory <<ConcreteCreator>> {
  #createCommissionCalculation(dealId: String, salesRepId: String, amount: BigDecimal): CommissionCalculation
  --
  <i>Creates "ACCELERATED-" prefixed calculations</i>
  <i>Applies 1.5x multiplier to base amount</i>
}

' Client
class Client <<Client>> {
  -factory: CommissionCalculatorFactory
  +processCommission(): void
}

' Relationships
CommissionCalculatorFactory <|-- StandardCommissionCalculatorFactory
CommissionCalculatorFactory <|-- BonusCommissionCalculatorFactory
CommissionCalculatorFactory <|-- AcceleratedCommissionCalculatorFactory

CommissionCalculatorFactory ..> CommissionCalculation : creates
StandardCommissionCalculatorFactory ..> CommissionCalculation : creates STANDARD-*
BonusCommissionCalculatorFactory ..> CommissionCalculation : creates BONUS-*
AcceleratedCommissionCalculatorFactory ..> CommissionCalculation : creates ACCELERATED-*

Client o--> "1" CommissionCalculatorFactory : uses
Client ..> CommissionCalculation : uses

' Component Notes
note right of CommissionCalculatorFactory
  <b>Abstract Creator</b>
  Declares the factory method that returns
  a Product object. Also contains template
  method that calls the factory method.

  <b>Key Methods:</b>
  • createCommissionCalculation() - Factory Method
    (abstract, implemented by subclasses)
  • calculateCommission() - Template Method
    (concrete, calls factory method then
    performs recalculation)

  <b>Pattern Principle:</b>
  Defers instantiation to subclasses
  while providing common workflow.
end note

note left of CommissionCalculation
  <b>Product</b>
  Defines the interface/class of
  objects the factory method creates.

  In this implementation, CommissionCalculation
  is the product. Different concrete creators
  create calculations with different IDs and
  commission amounts.

  <b>Variants:</b>
  • Standard (base amount)
  • Bonus (base + 10%)
  • Accelerated (base × 1.5)
end note

note bottom of StandardCommissionCalculatorFactory
  <b>Concrete Creator 1</b>
  Overrides factory method to return
  a standard CommissionCalculation.

  <b>Customization:</b>
  • Sets ID prefix: "STANDARD-"
  • Uses base amount as-is
  • Sets calculatedBy field

  <b>Factory Method Implementation:</b>
  Creates CommissionCalculation with
  standard commission rate.
end note

note bottom of BonusCommissionCalculatorFactory
  <b>Concrete Creator 2</b>
  Overrides factory method to return
  a bonus CommissionCalculation.

  <b>Customization:</b>
  • Sets ID prefix: "BONUS-"
  • Applies 10% bonus to base amount
  • Sets calculatedBy field

  <b>Factory Method Implementation:</b>
  Creates CommissionCalculation with
  bonus applied to base commission.
end note

note bottom of AcceleratedCommissionCalculatorFactory
  <b>Concrete Creator 3</b>
  Overrides factory method to return
  an accelerated CommissionCalculation.

  <b>Customization:</b>
  • Sets ID prefix: "ACCELERATED-"
  • Applies 1.5x multiplier to base amount
  • Sets calculatedBy field

  <b>Factory Method Implementation:</b>
  Creates CommissionCalculation with
  accelerated commission rate.
end note

note right of Client
  <b>Client Code</b>
  Works with Creator through abstract
  interface. Doesn't need to know the
  concrete class of the factory or
  the product.

  <b>Example Usage:</b>
  CommissionCalculatorFactory factory;
  factory = new BonusCommissionCalculatorFactory();
  CommissionCalculation calc = factory.calculateCommission(
    "DEAL-001",
    "SR-123",
    new BigDecimal("1000.00")
  );
  // Returns calculation with 10% bonus applied

  <b>Benefit:</b>
  Client can switch factory without
  changing its code.
end note

' Pattern Summary
note top of CommissionCalculatorFactory
  <b>Factory Method Pattern Components:</b>

  <b>Creator:</b> Declares factory method that
  returns Product object. May also define default
  implementation that returns a default Product.

  <b>ConcreteCreator:</b> Overrides factory method
  to return an instance of ConcreteProduct.

  <b>Product:</b> Defines interface of objects
  the factory method creates.

  <b>Template Method:</b> Creator contains
  template method (calculateCommission) that calls
  factory method and performs common operations
  (recalculate).

  <b>Key Benefits:</b>
  • Eliminates need to bind application-specific
    classes into code
  • Provides hooks for subclasses
  • Connects parallel class hierarchies
  • Follows Open/Closed Principle

  <b>Intent:</b>
  Define an interface for creating an object,
  but let subclasses decide which class to
  instantiate. Factory Method lets a class
  defer instantiation to subclasses.
end note

@enduml